{
  "note": "GA100 BAR0 fuse readout map, vendored from community research (kate-land/ga100vfi gpu0-capture data + GA100 public headers). Addresses only; no code dependency. `info` holds read-only state words; the STATUS_OPT_* ones are what prove a media engine is physically present, because hardware computes STATUS_OPT_* = OPT_DISABLE | OPT_DEFECTIVE (so STATUS == OPT means zero defects) and there is no *_DEFECTIVE register for NVDEC/NVJPG/OFA. dsov_status (0x820084) is the word ffmacro checks as DSOV_STATUS when deciding whether the card is inside a burn window; community floorsweep reports name the same word FUSE_DIS_SW_OVR. Together with en_sw_override (0x820040) they say whether the CTRL_OPT_* software-override route is alive at all: on datacenter GA100 it is not (0 / DSOV asserted outside the window), so the FF pool is the only lever for a floorsweep bit. The rest of `info` is the runtime half of the picture: the feature-override island (0x00823800-0x0082382c), the fused speed-select words (ss_*), the framebuffer geometry and ECC words, and the fuse-macro health/privilege words. Every address in this file has been read on two CMP 170HX cards; unmapped BAR0 comes back as 0xBADFxxxx, so a word is only listed when it returned a real value.",
